      {
        "t": 319.04,
        "who": "Dad",
        "text": "So where are all the Australians?"
      },
      {
        "t": 321.67,
        "who": "Globo",
        "text": "On the coast. Roughly eighty five percent live within about fifty kilometres of it. Mostly in the south east, plus Perth."
      },
      {
        "t": 329.84,
        "who": "Tara",
        "text": "Physical: the interior is arid, the coasts are wetter. Human: settlers came by sea, so ports grew into cities, with the jobs."
      },
      {
        "t": 338.26,
        "who": "Globo",
        "text": "Always use both kinds of factor, a named place, a figure, and a judgement."
      },
      {
        "t": 343.47,
        "who": "Globo",
        "text": "Locally, nobody lives in our nature reserves. That's planning, not physics. Scale changes the answer."
      },
      {
        "t": 350.38,
        "who": "Globo",
        "text": "In rich countries, technology makes human factors matter more. Dams, air conditioning, desalination."
      },
      {
        "t": 357.23,
        "who": "Tara",
        "text": "But physical limits never vanish. Desert cities like Las Vegas still worry about water."
      },
      {
        "t": 363.26,
        "who": "Dad",
        "text": "So my land just needs a dam, aircon, desalination, a port, jobs, and sixty years of planning."
      },
      {
        "t": 369.67,
        "who": "Tara",
        "text": "And a road."
      },
      {
        "t": 371.9,
        "who": "Globo",
        "text": "Recap. One. People are spread unevenly, mostly in Asia."
      },
      {
        "t": 375.92,
        "who": "Globo",
        "text": "Two. Density is population divided by area."
      },
      {
        "t": 379.18,
        "who": "Globo",
        "text": "Three. Physical factors, like relief, climate, water and soil."
      },
      {
        "t": 383.64,
        "who": "Globo",
        "text": "Four. Human factors, like jobs, transport and planning."
      },
      {
        "t": 387.66,
        "who": "Globo",
        "text": "Five. Explain with both, at the right scale. And never buy land with a seasonal tap."
      },
      {
        "t": 394.43,
        "who": "Dad",
        "text": "Good news. I sold the land. To someone who hates crowds."
      },
      {
        "t": 398.51,
        "who": "Mum",
        "text": "Sold it to whom?"
      },
      {
        "t": 400.07,
        "who": "Dad",
        "text": "A retired globe. Apparently he's moving out of the drawer."
      },
      {
        "t": 404.61,
        "who": "Globo",
        "text": "Two point two people per square kilometre. Finally. Some peace and quiet."
      }
