    "title": "Running A Class Census",
    "summary": "✘ LEADING question: pushes an answer · ✔ CLOSED: tick one box · Boxes cover everyone, no overlaps",
    "startSec": 164.25,
    "endSec": 247.0,
    "durationSec": 82.75,
    "src": "/videos/demography.mp4",
    "poster": "/videos/posters/demography.jpg",
    "captions": [
      {
        "t": 167.21,
        "who": "Dad",
        "text": "Uncle Hock! Question one. Don't you agree that I'm the most handsome man in this hawker centre?"
      },
      {
        "t": 173.63,
        "who": "Uncle",
        "text": "Is that a question or a threat?"
      },
      {
        "t": 176.73,
        "who": "Globo",
        "text": "That is a leading question. It pushes people towards one answer. Your data is now a soggy chip."
      },
      {
        "t": 183.15,
        "who": "Dad",
        "text": "Fine. Question two. How do you get here? He wrote, bus, sometimes walk, depends."
      },
      {
        "t": 188.64,
        "who": "Tara",
        "text": "Then you can't count it. Use a closed question. Main way here? Tick one box."
      },
      {
        "t": 193.88,
        "who": "Globo",
        "text": "The boxes must cover everyone and not overlap. One person, one box."
      },
      {
        "t": 198.57,
        "who": "Dad",
        "text": "Question three. What is your salary, your weight, and your Singpass password?"
      },
      {
        "t": 204.2,
        "who": "Globo",
        "text": "Ethics. Ask for consent. Let people skip. Keep it anonymous, and store it safely."
      },
      {
        "t": 212.47,
        "who": "Teacher",
        "text": "Tara, show us your class census. This is primary data. You collected it yourself."
      },
      {
        "t": 218.12,
        "who": "Tara",
        "text": "Twenty eight students. I counted with five bar gates. MRT nine, bus seven, walk six, car four, other two."
      },
      {
        "t": 225.29,
        "who": "Tara",
        "text": "Nine divided by twenty eight, times one hundred, is about thirty two point one percent who take the MRT."
      },
      {
        "t": 233.04,
        "who": "Globo",
        "text": "And can you say that thirty two percent of all students in Singapore take the MRT?"
      },
      {
        "t": 238.76,
        "who": "Tara",
        "text": "No. Twenty eight people, one class, one day. A small sample can't be generalised to the whole school, let alone Singapore."
      }
    ]
