    "title": "Pyramids And Dependency (Part 2)",
    "summary": "Young 0–14 · Working 15–64 · Elderly 65+ · Ratio = (0–14 + 65+) ÷ (15–64) × 100 · Niger: (49 + 3) ÷ 48 × 100 ≈ 108",
    "startSec": 308.15,
    "endSec": 433.25,
    "durationSec": 125.1,
    "src": "/videos/demography.mp4",
    "poster": "/videos/posters/demography.jpg",
    "captions": [
      {
        "t": 308.4,
        "who": "Dad",
        "text": "I've been thinking. I support this family. So I'm the dependant."
      },
      {
        "t": 313.06,
        "who": "Globo",
        "text": "No. You're the one they all depend on. Or so you claim."
      },
      {
        "t": 317.14,
        "who": "Globo",
        "text": "Young dependants are aged zero to fourteen. Working age is fifteen to sixty four. Elderly dependants are sixty five and over."
      },
      {
        "t": 325.71,
        "who": "Globo",
        "text": "The dependency ratio is young plus elderly, divided by working age, times one hundred. Dependants per hundred workers."
      },
      {
        "t": 333.82,
        "who": "Tara",
        "text": "So for Niger, forty nine plus three is fifty two. Divided by forty eight, times a hundred. About one hundred and eight."
      },
      {
        "t": 342.0,
        "who": "Globo",
        "text": "More dependants than workers. Japan's is about sixty seven. Lower, but mostly older people."
      },
      {
        "t": 348.39,
        "who": "Tara",
        "text": "Different problems. Niger needs schools and jobs. Japan needs pensions and carers."
      },
      {
        "t": 354.2,
        "who": "Dad",
        "text": "And Singapore?"
      },
      {
        "t": 355.66,
        "who": "Globo",
        "text": "Singapore is planning ahead. Around nineteen seventy, over ten working citizens for each older citizen. Now, about four."
      },
      {
        "t": 363.9,
        "who": "Globo",
        "text": "So the retirement age rose to sixty three in twenty twenty two, sixty four in twenty twenty six, with sixty five planned by twenty thirty."
      },
      {
        "t": 373.29,
        "who": "Tara",
        "text": "It's rough, though. Not every adult works, and many older people do."
      },
      {
        "t": 378.21,
        "who": "Dad",
        "text": "Like Uncle Hock. He's been sixty five for about ten years."
      },
      {
        "t": 383.34,
        "who": "Globo",
        "text": "Recap. One. Demography studies populations. Singapore's census is register based."
      },
      {
        "t": 389.09,
        "who": "Globo",
        "text": "Two. A sample must be fair. Random, systematic or stratified."
      },
      {
        "t": 393.56,
        "who": "Globo",
        "text": "Three. Closed questions, consent, and small samples can't speak for everyone."
      },
      {
        "t": 399.05,
        "who": "Globo",
        "text": "Four. Expansive pyramids are youthful, like Niger. Constrictive ones are ageing, like Japan and Singapore."
      },
      {
        "t": 406.4,
        "who": "Globo",
        "text": "Five. Dependency ratio is young plus elderly, over working age, times a hundred."
      },
      {
        "t": 413.03,
        "who": "Dad",
        "text": "The Rao Census is complete. One hundred percent of respondents agree I am handsome."
      }
    ]
